A common real shape: a mobile-first base plus two ALREADY-DISJOINT
`@media` ranges (tablet, desktop). v1 always wraps - no interval math -
so the tablet rule still gets a redundant `and not (...)` even though
the two ranges never overlap. Confirms correctness (unaffected output)
at the cost of extra bytes.

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml input.re > output.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl output.ml -o output.ml
  $ cat output.ml
  [@@@css "._a_7prbkv{margin:4px;}"]
  [@@@css
